"{\"blocks\":[{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"Among these shown options, I’d investigate the earlier-arriving Aeroplan itinerary first: it has the strongest combination of schedule and reported seat count. The tradeoff is an HKG connection and incomplete price information.\"},{\"k\":\"p\",\"r\":\"J8@2027-01-15T11:45-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-16T22:25\",\"n\":\"Earlier arrival\",\"v\":\"This economy award via HKG is reported with 9 seats and arrives 3 hours before the TPE option, with the same reported 65,000 Aeroplan points and CAD fee amount. Its downside: the award price scope is unknown, and the leg cabins aren’t specified.\"},{\"k\":\"a\",\"r\":\"J14@2027-01-15T23:15-08:00/SFO>BKK/E>2027-01-17T09:50\",\"n\":\"Later-departure alternative\",\"v\":\"Consider this HKG option if leaving late on January 15 matters: it departs 11 hours 30 minutes after the earlier-arriving choice and has the same reported points and fee amount, but arrives 11 hours 25 minutes later. It’s reported with 9 seats; availability still needs confirmation.\"},{\"k\":\"b\",\"r\":\"C3@2027-01-15T08:51-08:00/SFO>BKK\",\"n\":\"Cash baseline\",\"v\":\"The search returned $456 USD for a two-stop United/ANA itinerary via LAX and NRT. Its price scope is unknown, so treat it as a cash reference—not an all-in price or a like-for-like award valuation.\"},{\"k\":\"t\",\"v\":\"For both awards, the reported CAD fees are in minor units, and the price scope is unknown; points plus fees therefore don’t establish a complete award cost. The cash quote’s scope is also unknown. The search returned one traveler, but that does not establish the scope of any quote. Results were partial and may not be current; confirm itinerary details, award availability, and current prices with the providers before booking.\"}]}"
